# Geometry

Stubs: `.api/common/geometry/vector_2.lua`, `vector_3.lua`, `geometry.lua`.

## Vectors

```lua
---@type vec3
local vec3 = require("common/geometry/vector_3")

---@type vec2
local vec2 = require("common/geometry/vector_2")

local p = vec3.new(x, y, z)          -- new() takes no self
local d = p:dist_to(other)           -- instance methods are colon
```

- `new` has no `self` → **dot**. Everything with `fun(self: vec3, ...)` → **colon**.
- `vec2` also declares a `z` field despite the name. Do not treat its presence as proof a value is 3D.
- `vec3` adds `cross`, `project_2d`, `rotate_3d_radians`, the `dist_to_line_segment` family, and the ignore-z distances.
- Use `dist_to_ignore_z` / `squared_dist_to_ignore_z` for ground distance; plain `dist_to` includes height and will misjudge units above or below you.
- Prefer the squared variants for comparisons; do not add your own square root.
- `vector_2.dot_product(v1, v2)` is declared without `self` → dot.

Do not mix screen-space and world-space vectors. Confirm which space a function expects before passing a vector to it.

## Shapes — `geometry.lua` is type-only

`geometry.lua` declares `circle`, `rectangle`, `cone`, and `circle_data`, but has **no `return` and no require example**. Do not write `require("common/geometry/geometry")` on the assumption that it loads. Either obtain the shape from a verified source (see the IZI re-exports below) or confirm the runtime module layout first.

Shape class methods take `self` → colon:

```lua
local c = circle:create(center, radius)
local hit = c:get_enemies_inside()
c:draw_with_counter(#hit)
```

Also available per shape: `:is_inside(point, hitbox)`, `:get_units_inside(list)`, `:get_allies_inside(override?)`, `:draw()`. `circle` additionally has `:get_optimal_hit_position(search_center, search_radius, max_range, include_enemies, include_allies)` returning `circle_data`. `cone` has `:create_direction(center, direction, radius, angle)` and `:create_unit_frontal(unit, radius, angle)`, where direction comes from `obj:direction()`.

## IZI re-exports use different signatures

`izi_api` exposes callable geometry constructors whose parameters do **not** match the class `:create` methods:

| IZI call | Class method |
|---|---|
| `izi.circle(center, radius)` | `circle:create(center, radius)` |
| `izi.rectangle(min, max)` | `rectangle:create(origin, destination, width, length?)` |
| `izi.cone(origin, direction, angle, range)` | `cone:create(center, destination, radius, angle)` |

Note the cone argument order differs between the two. Pick one path per file and copy its exact signature. `izi.vec2` and `izi.vec3` are callable the same way (`izi.vec3(x, y, z)`).

## Prediction enums are not shapes

`spell_prediction.geometry_type` (`CIRCLE` / `RECTANGLE` / `CONE`) selects a prediction model. IZI cast options take `geometry` as `"CIRCLE"|"LINE"|number`. Neither is a drawable shape object. Do not pass an enum where a shape is expected, or invent a `LINE` shape class — the shape stub has no such class.

## Never invent

Vector methods, shape constructors, argument orders, or a shape module path that no stub declares.
